          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb167ca839ab9aa67e725e0e1cd06a9ba7564f83ef3c87955db754b6d30a3cd8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_950ded5b702048aa9bf41705a8a652a1",
      "statement": "A ChannelHandle stores an absolute float offset into the buffer rather than a section-local index so reading costs no layout arithmetic, and it carries the LayoutHash it was bound against because such a handle would otherwise address arbitrary floats in a buffer built from a different layout; every accessor asserts the match in assertion builds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/ChannelHandle.cs#L3-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3a08e31cc7236002e7199f41f6defa54c51dc1c1bd86a66c12240dfbbc8320e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Tests/Editor/PoseLayoutTests.cs#L327-L349",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a99d6855fc8684b37ab763217fcc380afc0506f7e0b67e4e442f602b4be41b29:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3efda7b56dc147baa4db58ad84c3ae20",
      "statement": "LayoutHash is claimed as the exact equivalence class rather than an approximation — it covers every channel's content and, for pose layouts, the skeleton — so equal hashes mean identical offsets, and because CopyFrom asserts on the same hash, handle validity and copy compatibility agree by construction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/ChannelHandle.cs#L3-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3a08e31cc7236002e7199f41f6defa54c51dc1c1bd86a66c12240dfbbc8320e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/State/StateBuffer.cs#L107-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61d1303efac4e2ddeb1f100b5fe6702c7e229bf524c43ec979d9f6053c0ad4d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_307f2f40a7da41748415742976677533",
      "statement": "A ChannelDescriptor carries two hashes deliberately: GetHashCode answers which channel this is and keys the offset table so binding never has to restate descriptive metadata, while GetContentHash also folds in space and rotation representation and feeds the layout hash — so two layouts differing only in a channel's space address identically yet are not interchangeable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/ChannelDescriptor.cs#L5-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2b158880d0168160ed75169bb57b330612491972bc11b7b9f083ed820b9ed07:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Tests/Editor/PoseLayoutTests.cs#L315-L325",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfb7700e44db1a23b210a5dde9a77ebbf062deead17cf69ac7ca05a13b588913:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f31b6f7f048d4d629918bc58d5216560",
      "statement": "Section keys are const ints rather than enum ordinals because section order is a buffer-layout contract, and deriving it from a declaration order would let a cosmetic reorder — such as sorting the enum alphabetically — silently move pose data with no compile error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/ChannelTypes.cs#L3-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e7e563d1118618b8cb082a23fdf43ce8f933729a05752f10dd429128b5ba5b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b9ac387ab4546c1930c30e859fa6e17",
      "statement": "Channel kinds outside the six built-ins must use a section key greater than Bool, which keeps them in a contiguous tail after the built-in sections; PoseLayout.Build throws when a non-built-in channel claims a reserved key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/ChannelTypes.cs#L3-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e7e563d1118618b8cb082a23fdf43ce8f933729a05752f10dd429128b5ba5b6:"
