    {
      "id": "claim_7011a294722e460da45baaa0b68a1f4b",
      "statement": "Booleans are stored as one float, written as 0 or 1 and read back with a 0.5 threshold, which keeps a buffer a single homogeneous float array and is what makes flat copies and single-call numpy reads possible.",
